Write ADR defining verified issuer+subject -> internal user, request-scoped identity, user-owned config/runtime/store contracts, client grants, immutable runtime generations, session identity binding, activation recovery, and single-process SQLite assumption. All views including default/search and same-name routes resolve from current OAuth user; no global operational fallback or workspace indirection. Specify supported change classes and trusted static-token/stdio compatibility. Acceptance: interfaces, schema, state machine, failure semantics, migration ownership, and endpoint compatibility documented.
